{
  "about": "Rows are read by polling and hooks arrive at once, so a hook of the turn a prompt sent through amux began can land before that prompt's row. A hook makes no row, so nothing waits: the prompt's row precedes its turn's rows in the transcript, and the calls follow it. A tool server's form owns its item from its hook. A prompt Claude folds into a turn already running is reflected by its queued-command row, so later reflections keep their own input ids.",
